  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 129 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nFriday through Monday:\n\nFriday and Friday evening will be dry now, as the forecast has\ntrended drier each day. This is due to high pressure remaining in\nplace over the lower Great Lakes longer. Low pressure developing\nover the Dakotas on Friday will lift into northern MN. We can\nexpect increasing southerly winds in southern WI, along with an\nuptick in temperatures and dewpoints (upper 70s/lower 60s).\n\nThe strongest forcing will be over Upper Michigan as the low\ntracks overhead and the low level jet focuses there. The other \narea of forcing will arrive with a mid level shortwave trough\ntracking from the central Plains to IA and northern IL late \nFriday night through Saturday morning. There are hints from the\nmodels that the precip associated with these two forcing areas\nwill split right around southern WI. \n\nWinds will shift to the west Saturday afternoon behind the surface\ntrough, but gusts will be less than 20 mph. Saturday will be our\nwarmest and most humid day with highs closer to 80 and dewpoints\npotentially pooling ahead of the trough/cold front to values in \nthe upper 60s. Temperatures will fall into the 50s Saturday night\nbehind that front. \n\nA stronger mid level trough crossing the Northern Rockies on\nSunday will help push that front back up through Southern WI.\nLight rain may accompany this warm front during the day, but\nmodels are trending later with the storm chances. The important\nfeature to note this far out is that there will be a prominent\nwarm front with the nose of the low level jet present. This will\nalign with the right entrance region of an upper jet and a low-\namplitude mid level shortwave (weak intensity). The location of \nthis warm front/llj nose is still uncertain. A storm complex \nshould develop along this front Sunday evening and there should be\nsufficient shear and instability for some severe storms, but we \nare not sure if they will be exactly in southern WI. \n\nThe surface trough crossing WI on Monday afternoon or night could\ntrigger another round of showers and storms. \n\nCronce\nWFO MKX",
